"""Round 2 (2026-10-22): sounds and words where Lumi must say NOTHING or must not act: music with whisper's
hallucinations (caption credits, "Thank you for watching", "구독과 좋아요", "-", "...", "감사합니다.", "Lumi." written for
music), TV / PA announcements, caption credits in other languages, coughs and sneezes, fillers, laughter, visitors
talking to each other (with "stop", "go", "look", "follow", "sing" between themselves and no wake word), words said to
someone else during a talk, Lumi's own voice heard back (whole, cut, misheard), stray words in an empty room before or
after a goodbye. Written blind from docs/14 and docs/WORK_PLAN.md only.

CASES = [{"heard", "kind", "ctx", "expect"}] (round 1's format)
- heard: the text whisper returned ("" when it returned nothing).
- kind: music | tv | caption | cough | filler | laugh | others_talking | echo | empty_room.
- ctx: {"session": "none" (nobody talking with Lumi, no wake word) | "open" (a talk is going on) | "just_ended" (a
  goodbye was said a moment ago), "lumi_said": Lumi's last line or None, "people": people in view, "speech_s":
  seconds of speech the VAD found in the sound (0 for music / noise), "from_lumi_speaker": True when the sound is
  Lumi's own voice coming back through the microphone}.
- expect: "nothing" = no words, no motion, no goodbye, no greeting, no "say it again"; "no_action" = a short friendly
  line is fine, but nothing moves and the talk is not ended (fillers, laughs and words to someone else while a talk
  is open).

held-out: only scored, never read by whoever fixes the code.
"""

